{"action_id":null,"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.05b977f28b68c771dbfcd320.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Paragraph 10 is read with the supplied ownership-record requirement and paragraph 14 assurance provisions.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.05b977f28b68c771dbfcd320.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Operational evidence is assessed against an applicable standard, rather than an invented guarantee against every failure.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":null,"candidate_id":"candidate.9899b0cc76824211ab1ba7414fb0dcce","controlled_language":"Read with the express requirement to ensure proper ownership records and operational compatibility, paragraph 10 can instead be understood as requiring the Product Provider to discharge substantive responsibility for the arrangement. A supported fulfillment conclusion would require evidence of retained accountability, effective supervisory conduct and operational and record-keeping performance meeting the applicable standard. Formal authority or an assertion of responsibility is insufficient; supervision is evidence of performance, not an automatic substitute for it. The intermediary due-diligence and prior satisfaction provisions concern separate actors and controls and cannot themselves establish provider fulfillment. The excerpt does not resolve whether every failure defeats fulfillment or whether an applicable standard permits a qualified assessment.","disposition_reason":"Unreviewed interpretation proposal","family_ids":["modality"],"generation_phase":"BLIND_INITIAL","issue_ids":[],"parent_id":null,"probability_of_legal_correctness":null,"revision_reason":"This reading makes substantive performance part of fulfillment of the responsibility requirement itself. Under the allocation reading, retained responsibility can be established separately from failed performance; here, authority and diligent supervision alone cannot establish fulfillment where required outcomes are absent.","run_id":"run.8adc12b432874c5bb1e8b4730a0ab93f","scheduling_priority":0,"schema_version":"interpretation.v1","score_purpose":"INVESTIGATION_PRIORITY_ONLY","source_packet_hash":"d74180e126dda06342060a17b37c3227fc695e9fc0f0d5ce68b187d7cb8bc612","source_unit_ids":["dc689bdf0ffcf.u0.0","dc689bdf0ffcf.u1.224","dc689bdf0ffcf.u11.3045","dc689bdf0ffcf.u2.729","dc689bdf0ffcf.u3.944","dc689bdf0ffcf.u4.1185"],"status":"ACTIVE","subject_unit":"Paragraph 10 and footnote 1: substantive discharge of responsibility"}